+# Q3 2026 Operating Brief
+
+## Executive summary
+
+Q3 was a solid quarter financially, with $720,000 in revenue against $464,000 in verified
+spend, producing an operating surplus of $256,000. Support held a close rate near 93.7%
+against 1,250 opened tickets, and security resolved 95.0% of the 80 incidents it detected.
+The delivery team's project begun on 2026-10-05 tracks to a launch on 2026-10-23 once
+weekends and the company planning-day holiday are correctly accounted for. Several figures
+published in the underlying source packets do not match the underlying itemized data and
+are called out below for leadership awareness.
+
+## Key figures
+
+| Metric | Value |
+|---|---:|
+| Q3 revenue | $720,000 |
+| Q3 spend | $464,000 |
+| Operating surplus | $256,000 |
+| Support close rate | 93.7% |
+| Launch date | 2026-10-23 |
+| Security resolution rate | 95.0% |
+
+## Notes
+
+- **Finance spend discrepancy:** the finance packet's summary line states total Q3 spend as
+  $463,250, but the itemized spend categories (Payroll $286,400 + Infrastructure $81,750 +
+  Contractors $64,200 + Facilities $31,650) sum to $464,000, a $750 difference. The figure
+  above uses the itemized total; finance should reconcile the summary line.
+- **Support close rate discrepancy:** the support dashboard reports a 96.4% close rate, but
+  1,171 closed of 1,250 opened tickets computes to 93.7%. This is a meaningful gap worth
+  escalating to the support team to confirm which figure (and which underlying counts) is
+  correct.
+- **Delivery launch date discrepancy:** the delivery summary records the launch date as
+  2026-10-22. Recomputing the phase schedule from the 2026-10-05 start date (Discovery 3
+  days, Build 6 days, QA 4 days, Release 1 day; each phase inclusive of its duration in
+  business days, next phase starting the next business day, weekends and the 2026-10-12
+  company planning-day holiday excluded) yields a launch date of 2026-10-23, one business
+  day later than recorded. Leadership should confirm the correct launch date before it is
+  communicated externally.
+- **Security figures:** the 95.0% resolution rate (76 of 80 incidents) matches the packet's
+  own summary and required no correction.
